    "done_when": "Read section 35 of crew-runtime-positive-controls first, and reproduce or rule out its unconfirmed cause (a producer re-exec interrupting the reflex launch) before changing code; state which in the evidence. In reckon/crew/recovery.py, a pointer still at a pre-spawn phase (starting, launching, launcher or dispatching) with no pid and no worker record, stream or stderr in its run directory, older than a bound stated as a named constant, is classified as a stranded launch rather than in flight. The review reflex discards it with a recorded reason and composes the review again. tests/test_stranded_launch_releases_its_claim.py, in a temporary RECKON_HOME, builds such a pointer and asserts both the release and the recomposed review; a pointer inside the bound stays in flight. Existing recovery tests that reach the pre-spawn phases keep passing; grep tests/ for _PRE_SPAWN_PHASES and starting to build the gate. Record the outcome in docs/evidence/fragments/crew-runtime-positive-controls/stranded-launch-releases-its-claim.html. Run `date -u` first and treat that instant as your start; your deadline is 60 minutes later. Write your manifest before starting any long command. Run both gate arms with pytest-xdist (-n 8 --timeout=300), never serially. Run the base arm, from a `git archive` extraction of your base under /tmp in a directory named for this run, and then the head arm, each in the foreground: a background command dies when your turn ends. Keep the gate to the test files that reach your change, tens of files rather than hundreds. Each arm uses its own basetemp outside any repository and writes to its own new log path, which it never overwrites. Each arm is recorded as JSON carrying completed true and a literal command with absolute paths and no angle-bracket placeholder. Each log names its revision on the first line as revision= followed by the full sha, and ends with a bare line reading EXIT= followed by the exit code. The head arm adds no failure id; any added id means status blocked, naming each id. ruff check and ruff format --check over the changed Python paths report no finding the base did not. Scratch goes under /tmp in a directory named for this run and is deleted before status complete. The turn ends once the manifest reads complete or blocked.",
